# Desktop overlay UX

## Shape and surface
- One cream `#shell` that morphs — do not add a separate left cream card beside the EXP rail.
- Boxy rounded corners (`~14px`), not pill/`border-radius: 999px` on the shell.
- EXP rail stays on the docked edge (right/left/top); content lives inside the same shell.

## Open / close motion
- Prefer function-driven stages over stepped frame `setBounds` loops.
- Open: extend **down** (tall strip) then **out** (full width), then fade content in.
- Close: fade content out, then reverse (narrow, then shorten).
- Use native `setBounds(bounds, true)` on macOS when motion is allowed; respect reduced motion (instant bounds, no waits).
- Keep `panelToggleSeq` so rapid toggles cancel stale timeouts.

## Pet
- Anchor the pet beside the EXP rail (`barThickness`), not the far edge of the open panel window.
- Pet stays click-through; handle-only dragging; no bottom dock target (left/right/top only).

## Do not
- Invent XP or change session/score APIs for overlay polish.
- Leave a large transparent window after close that blocks other apps.
